insights into the pathogenicity of <italic>Burkholderia pseudomallei</italic>.</article-title><source>Nat Rev Microbiol</source><volume>4</volume><fpage>272</fpage><lpage>282</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16541135</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000178-Sandford1"><label>6</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sandford</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><year>1985</year><article-title>Melioidosis : Practice and principles of infectious diseases;</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Mandell</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name><name><surname>Douglas</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name><name><surname>Bennet</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Churchill Livingstone</publisher-name><fpage>1250</fpage><lpage>1254</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000178-Choy1"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Choy</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Mayo</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Janmaat</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Currie</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Animal melioidosis in Australia.</article-title><source>Acta Trop</source><volume>74</volume><fpage>153</fpage><lpage>158</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10674644</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000178-Gan1"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gan</surname><given-names>YH</given-names></name><name><surname>Chua</surname><given-names>KL</given-names></name><name><surname>Chua</surname><given-names>HH</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Hii</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Characterization of <italic>Burkholderia pseudomallei</italic> infection and identification of novel virulence factors using a <italic>Caenorhabditis elegans</italic> host system.</article-title><source>Mol Microbiol</source><volume>44</volume><fpage>1185</fpage><lpage>1197</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12068805</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000178-Howard1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Howard</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Inglis</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Disinfection of <italic>Burkholderia pseudomallei</italic> in potable water.</article-title><source>Water Res</source><volume>39</volume><fpage>1085</fpage><lpage>1092</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15766962</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000178-Inglis1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Inglis</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Foster</surname><given-names>NF</given-names></name><name><surname>Gal</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Powell</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Mayo</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Preliminary report on the northern Australian melioidosis environmental surveillance project.</article-title><source>Epidemiol Infect</source><volume>132</volume><fpage>813</fpage><lpage>820</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15473143</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000178-Ketterer1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ketterer</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Webster</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name><name><surname>Shield</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Arthur</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Blackall</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1986</year><article-title>Melioidosis in intensive piggeries in south eastern Queensland.</article-title><source>Aust Vet J</source><volume>63</volume><fpage>146</fpage><lpage>149</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3753342</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000178-Brook1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brook</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name><name><surname>Currie</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Desmarchelier</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Isolation and identification of <italic>Burkholderia pseudomallei</italic> from soil using selective culture techniques and the polymerase chain reaction.</article-title><source>J Appl Microbiol</source><volume>82</volume><fpage>589</fpage><lpage>596</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9172400</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000178-Dance1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dance</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Ecology of <italic>Burkholderia pseudomallei</italic> and the interactions between environmental <italic>Burkholderia</italic> spp. and human-animal hosts.</article-title><source>Acta Trop</source><volume>74</volume><fpage>159</fpage><lpage>168</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10674645</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000178-Finkelstein1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Finkelstein</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Atthasampunna</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Chulasamay